    "title": "Minimum Number of Visited Cells in a Grid",
    "category": "Queue",
    "difficulty": "Hard",
    "problemStatement": "You are given an m \u00d7 n grid of non-negative integers. Starting from the top-left cell, you may move: Right by at most grid[i][j] cells. Down by at most grid[i][j] cells. Return the minimum number of visited cells needed to reach the bottom-right cell. If the destination cannot be reached, return -1.",
    "input": "Integers m and n Grid of integers.",
    "output": "A single integer.",
    "constraints": "1 <= m, n <= 10^5 m \u00d7 n <= 10^5 0 <= grid[i][j] <= 10^5"
